/-!
# The bounded-generator locus cut out by a Fitting ideal

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tags 0C3C, 0C3F and 05P8(2); More on Algebra,
Tag 07ZC(1),(3),(4) (blueprint: lem-trf-fitting-ideal-generate-locally).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- The affine kernel-minor ideals glue to `fittingIdealSheaf F r`. Its support is the
underlying closed set of `(fittingIdealSheaf F r).subscheme`, whose canonical inclusion
is a closed immersion. The complement represents the locus where an arbitrary pullback
is locally generated by at most `r` sections. At each point, membership in the complement,
the ideal stalk being the whole local ring, generation on a neighbourhood, and generation
of the module stalk by at most `r` elements are equivalent. Families of exactly `r`
sections/elements encode "at most `r`" by padding with zeros, including `r = 0`.
Surjectivity of the inclusion of ideal stalks expresses equality with the local ring.
Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tags 0C3C, 0C3F, 05P8(2); More on Algebra, Tag 07ZC.
(blueprint: lem-trf-fitting-ideal-generate-locally)

Proof plan:
0. By `lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine` the section module on every
   affine open is finite. Presentation independence and localization from
   `lem-trf-fitting-ideal-independence-base-change` make the affine supremum in
   `fittingIdealSheaf` equal to every presentation ideal and compatible with basic opens.
   Hence `IdealSheafData.ofIdeals` recovers those very ideals.
1. On an affine neighbourhood `U = Spec A`, identify `F|U` with the tilde of its sections
   using `lem-weil-pbc-affine-tilde-gamma-adjunction`, and its stalk with the localization
   using `lem-sbc-affine-module-germ-localization`. The Fitting ideal localizes by
   `lem-trf-fitting-ideal-independence-base-change`; the zero-set dictionary
   `lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-ideal-zero-set-affine` identifies being off its support
   with the ideal stalk being the whole local ring.
2. If a generating `(n-r)`-minor is invertible at the point, write its kernel rows as
   `(C D)`. The adjugate identity `lem-weil-pbc-matrix-adjugate-identity` solves
   `Cx + Dy = 0` for the first `n-r` generators, leaving `r` generators on `D(det C)`.
   Their germs span each stalk there by the affine germ-localization identification;
   local expressions glue to the sheaf-surjectivity in
   `def-weil-pbc-generating-sections`. If `n ≤ r`, use the original generators.
3. Neighbourhood generators give stalk generators by taking germs. Conversely, a
   surjection from `r` copies of the local ring gives unit `r`th Fitting ideal by
   convention. Presentation independence and localization identify it with the stalk
   ideal from step 1. This proves the pointwise equivalences without finite presentation.
4. For any `g : T ⟶ S`, work on affine charts. By
   `lem-weil-pbc-tilde-pullback-base-change` and
   `lem-weil-pbc-spec-module-tilde-sections`, pullback is tilde of the tensor module.
   Tensoring a finite generating family gives a finite generating family. Thus the
   pullback is finite type and quasi-coherent, and its Fitting ideal is the extended
   original ideal by `lem-trf-fitting-ideal-independence-base-change`, with no flatness.
5. A prime contains the extended ideal iff its contraction contains the original.
   Step 3 on `T` therefore makes local generation everywhere equivalent to image
   containment in the complement. Apply
   `lem-weil-pbc-morphism-factors-through-open-subscheme` to get precisely the
   factorization through that open; a factorization conversely gives image containment.
-/
theorem fitting_ideal_generate_locally (S : Scheme.{u}) (F : S.Modules)
    [F.IsFiniteType] [F.IsQuasicoherent] (r : ℕ) :
    (∀ (U : S.affineOpens) (n : ℕ)
      (π : (Fin n → Γ(S, U.1)) →ₗ[Γ(S, U.1)] Γ(F, U.1)),
      Function.Surjective π → (fittingIdealSheaf F r).ideal U =
        π.presentationFittingIdeal r) ∧
    (∀ (T : Scheme.{u}) (g : T ⟶ S),
      (∀ t : T, ∃ U : T.Opens, t ∈ U ∧
        ∃ s : ULift.{u} (Fin r) → (((tensorPullback g).obj F).over U).sections,
          Epi ((((tensorPullback g).obj F).over U).freeHomEquiv.symm s)) ↔
      ∃ h : T ⟶ Scheme.Opens.toScheme (X := S) (fittingIdealSheaf F r).support.compl,
        h ≫ Scheme.Opens.ι (X := S) (fittingIdealSheaf F r).support.compl = g) ∧
    (∀ x : S,
      (x ∉ (fittingIdealSheaf F r).support ↔
        Function.Surjective ((RingedSpace.moduleStalkFunctor S.toRingedSpace x).map
          (fittingIdealSheaf F r).toModulesι).hom) ∧
      (x ∉ (fittingIdealSheaf F r).support ↔
        ∃ U : S.Opens, x ∈ U ∧
          ∃ s : ULift.{u} (Fin r) → (F.over U).sections,
            Epi ((F.over U).freeHomEquiv.symm s)) ∧
      (x ∉ (fittingIdealSheaf F r).support ↔
        ∃ s : Fin r → (RingedSpace.moduleStalkFunctor S.toRingedSpace x).obj F,
          Submodule.span (S.presheaf.stalk x) (Set.range s) = ⊤)) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
